WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.320
Critics and fans alike love the&nbsp;
final installment of the "Guardians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.940
of the Galaxy" trilogy, but one iconic&nbsp;
accessory was conspicuously absent from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.960
the blockbuster. And now, director James&nbsp;
Gunn has weighed in on making that call.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.880
Star-Lord and his space buddies surpassed&nbsp;
expectations for "Guardians of the Galaxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:23.640
Vol. 3," earning huge box office numbers as the&nbsp;
Marvel Cinematic Universe underdogs. This final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:28.860
“Guardians” entry gives a poignant farewell to&nbsp;
its titular misfits, and many viewers praised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:34.140
James Gunn for his perfect swan song. However,&nbsp;
some fans wondered about its finer details.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.140
One common question on Twitter&nbsp;
after the film’s release was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.980
“What happened to Star-Lord’s helmet?”&nbsp;
which he never wears in the threequel.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.180
"Well, that's a good question."
We know he gets a new one between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.520
“Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2” and “Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.540
Infinity War,” but its status in his&nbsp;
latest adventure puzzled many fans.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:56.220
Fortunately, we have an answer for why Quill’s&nbsp;
essential headwear — and his clip-on rocket&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:00.360
boots — were missing. Gunn recently explained&nbsp;
that because of the urgency of his mission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:05.040
to rescue his best friend Rocket Raccoon,&nbsp;
he left his iconic Guardians gear behind.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.160
On Twitter, where he often shares&nbsp;
insights directly with fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.480
Gunn set the record straight about Quill&nbsp;
not wearing a helmet in "Vol. 3." in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.260
tongue-in-cheek reply. In response&nbsp;
to one user's question, he joked,

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.220
"It's in his desk drawer [on] Knowhere. He&nbsp;
had to get out of there fast as you know!"

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.840
While this lack of helmet can be easily&nbsp;
forgiven, his enhanced footwear accessories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.200
very well could have made for handy&nbsp;
tools on his quest. As it turns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.880
Gunn cleared up this particular matter as&nbsp;
well, in a less jokey manner, revealing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.740
the Guardians' technology has advanced by leaps&nbsp;
and bounds, all thanks to Rocket. Gunn posted,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.040
"The rockets that clip onto his&nbsp;
boots are far inferior to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.100
jet packs Rocket has made them so&nbsp;
they're not around at all anymore."

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.560
Time and a supersmart raccoon, then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.920
are the simple answers to this apparent&nbsp;
change to Star-Lord's character.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.420
Even so, there may still be a chance that we'll&nbsp;
see Quill back in his old gear down the line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.080
given that the ending of "Vol. 3"&nbsp;
confirms Chris Pratt's MCU future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.220
Otherwise, a lonely helmet somewhere on&nbsp;
Knowhere may no longer have an owner.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:06.300
While Gunn may have jokingly explained&nbsp;
away Star-Lord's in-universe mentality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:10.080
behind traveling without his helmet, some&nbsp;
fans in a Reddit thread about this subject&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.320
have proposed additional theories&nbsp;
about the decision. Gunn, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.860
could have easily justified keeping&nbsp;
the iconic headwear in "Vol. 3," but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.520
chose instead to alter the character in&nbsp;
a way plenty of fans found noticeable.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:24.540
In the thread's top comment, for example,&nbsp;
one user argued that Star-Lord's lack of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.500
gear emphasizes his singular focus on&nbsp;
saving Rocket. Meanwhile, another fan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.940
proposed that the film may simply be trying&nbsp;
to maximize Chris Pratt's on-screen face time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:37.440
in the same manner Steve Rogers inexplicably&nbsp;
fights without a helmet during big moments in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.060
the "Avengers" films prior to Chris Evans' Marvel&nbsp;
Cinematic Universe exit. Another user wrote,

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:46.260
"I like this interpretation some people had&nbsp;
where Peter wanted to distance himself from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:49.440
Star Lord. Ties in nicely with how&nbsp;
he went back to Earth at the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.960
to his roots as a human&nbsp;
being and with his grandpa."

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.860
Since he leaves the Guardians team at the&nbsp;
end of the film, it's entirely possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:00.300
then, that Peter Quill will remain unmasked&nbsp;
in his future appearances — a new direction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:04.020
for his character as he remains a&nbsp;
big part of the post-"Guardians" MCU.

